========================================================================
        DESCRIPTION
========================================================================

Matlab mex implementation of dasslc, solver for differential algebraic
equations of any index.

Version 1.2, May 2008

Author: Argimiro R. Secchi <arge@enq.ufrgs.br>
	Department of Chemical Engineering
	Federal University of Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil

Based on Steinar Hauan <hauan@cmu.edu>

This code is published under the BSD License
http://www.opensource.org/licenses/bsd-license.php

It can be dowloaded at
http://www.enq.ufrgs.br/enqlib/numeric
with the Version 3.3 of dasslc.
========================================================================
        INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS
========================================================================
uncomment #define MATLAB in dasslc.h

MATLAB up to 5.3
mex -V4 -output dasslc dasslc2ml.c dasslc.c

MATLAB version > 5.3
mex -output dasslc dasslc2ml.c dasslc.c
mex -output dasslcss dasslc2mlss.c dasslc.c

========================================================================
        LIST OF FILES 
========================================================================

    README.dasslc2ml: this file

    dasslc.m        : short mex interface documentation (from matlab)
    dasslc.dll	    : compiled mex file for windows
    dasslc2ml.c	    : mex gateway function
    dasslc.c	    : the solver
    dasslc.h	    : solver header file
    dasslc.pdf	    : solver manual

    pend.m	    : residual function of classical pendulum
    jacpend.m       : iteration matrix of pendulum problem
    test_pend.m     : calling script of pendulum problem

    dydt.m          : residual function of simple example
    test.m          : calling script of simple example

    dydt1.m         : minimal residual function of simple example
    test1.m         : calling script of simple example with minimal args

